 (1) build_backend is asymmetric — _build_cloud calls assert_cloud_scope_ready(s) at build, but _build_datacenter defers all validation to the lazy _LazyDataCenterClient (by design, so composing needs no [agents] extra/JIRA_PAT). Decide whether the DC path should assert non-secret scope readiness (url/project) at build for symmetry while keeping PAT/network lazy. (2) assert_cloud_scope_ready enforces JIRA_USER-must-be-email and non-empty query_project, which the legacy ambient assert_env_ready does not — the same JiraBackend fails-closed differently by path. These stricter checks catch real misconfigurations (email is required for Cloud Basic auth; empty project would query every project), and real Cloud deployments satisfy them, so this is deferred as a deliberate parity decision rather than rushed into S2. Choose: keep stricter (document as intended tightening) or relax to match legacy.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"4698-d85c-b1a3-40d3","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-04 follow-up: align reconciler Cloud/DC fail-closed symmetry and scope-vs-ambient readiness parity","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["417e1a2b-70e0-408b-bf99-222255d3c1f8","3948d4b4-be8c-4c0f-b8a9-f4f249d39d8d"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787029931161347001,"uuid":"9b94cc06-e0c1-470e-884b-a661c126b19d"}